Halacha Four

Part Two &mdash; Sections &#x05D6;&ndash;&#x05D9;

And therefore the essential completion of the clarification is through the Chalah separated from the dough made of flour and water &mdash; the waters of da&rsquo;as [knowledge] and Torah drawn upon the flour. And through this one gathers and collects it and kneads it and makes dough. And then it is obligated in Chalah: to give the raishis to the Kohen who is composed of ben v&rsquo;talmid, through which the entire dough is included in the aforementioned aspect, in the aspect of Torah and da&rsquo;as, through which all the sparks ascend etc. as mentioned. And therefore Chalah is practiced even now outside the Land of Israel, because through Chalah comes the essential clarification as mentioned.

Section Ten &middot; &#x05D9;

And this is why the Torah portion of Chalah is juxtaposed with the Torah portion of the Spies (Meraglim) in the portion Shelach Lecha (Bamidbar 13&ndash;15). For the Spies blemished the Land of Israel and blemished the aspect of the illumination of ben v&rsquo;talmid &mdash; as is understood from the aforementioned Torah. For they passed through the Land of Israel when it was still in exile under the hand of the seven nations. And when they came there they were seized with fears, and they were placed there in a state of smallness and lowliness (katnus v&rsquo;shiplut), in the aspect of exile, as it is written: &ldquo;and we were in our own eyes as grasshoppers&rdquo; (vanhi v&rsquo;ainaynu kachagavim) etc. (Bamidbar 13:33).

